{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261116T081910Z_dev-02_staged_80e3", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "No. The dSph gamma-ray limit is the approximate one-sided 95% upper limit, set where 2[ln L_max − ln L(⟨σv⟩₉₅)] = 2.71 (a TS drop of 2.71). It is profiled over each dwarf's J-factor normalization (log10 s), which carries a Gaussian prior from the stellar-kinematic J-factor uncertainty, over log10 s in [−3, 3]. The AMS-02 antiproton limit is the upper endpoint of the ΔQ ≤ 3.84 region, where Q = −2 ln L. The paper calls 3.84 the nominal 95% interval threshold for one parameter of interest and says it differs from the one-sided 2.71 prescription. It is profiled over the Galactic diffusive-halo half-height L, with a Gaussian penalty in log10 L centred on 4.96 kpc with σ = 0.197, over 1–12 kpc.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.2"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.3"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "5"}]}, "turns": 7, "seconds": 15.076, "tool_calls": 7, "tool_result_chars": 29250, "input_tokens": 16, "output_tokens": 1399, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 15960, "cache_read_input_tokens": 52531, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-16T08:19:26+00:00"}
